body:
In the schema-fetching effect, the `fetchObjectSchema()` function contains a `!dataSource` error path, but it’s never reached because `fetchObjectSchema()` is only called when `schema.objectName && dataSource`. When `objectName` is set and inline fields are not provided, but `dataSource` is missing, the code currently just `setLoading(false)` and renders an empty form (no error). Consider setting an explicit error in this branch (or calling `fetchObjectSchema()` whenever `schema.objectName` is present so the existing error handling runs) so the UI shows a clear failure state instead of a blank form.
```suggestion
    } else if (schema.objectName) {
      // Fetch schema using objectName; fetchObjectSchema will handle missing dataSource
      fetchObjectSchema();
    } else if (!hasInlineFields) {
      // No objectName and no inline fields — cannot proceed
      setError(new Error('Object name is required when inline fields are not provided'));
```
